// FoxSDR Slint front end - THE MAIN SCREEN (phase 1 of the port, docs/engine-stage4.md 6.36).
//
// Workbench.dc.html, 1440 x 900, top to bottom: title bar 36 | receiver strip 104 | (sound-muted banner 28 when
// a plugin mutes) | body (icon rail 64 | sections panel 296 | centre: tab row 32, spectrum, splitter 6,
// waterfall 270) | status bar 28. Everything shown is a property the C++ host fills from the C API table
// (read_state / read_list / read_spectrum once per tick); every key, gesture and shortcut is a callback the host
// turns into a submit() on the table. The window is frameless on every platform (the IA's 36 px title bar) and
// the host moves, sizes, minimises and maximises it from the chrome callbacks.
//
// The inventory (main-window-frame, spectrum-waterfall) is walked row by row in docs/slint-port-tick.md: every
// row is here, relocated here as the Workbench IA says (deck meters into the status bar and the level line,
// mode keys onto the strip, status cards into the status bar), or deferred with its reason in that list.

